  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training for urban leadership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNITAS promotes organisation and participation within communities to support them to have a critical analysis of their reality and engage with actors such as the government to improve it. Through educational activities they work to raise awareness within the community of common problems and what work can be done to pressure for them to be resolved. They also support them to network and collaborate with other social movements. UNITAS is an umbrella organisation of 28 NGOs in Bolivia. It provides a forum in which groups in this sector can discuss, collaborate and lobby on development issues at national level.  This programme trains poor urban communities to intervene policy-making to secure funding for the development of deprived communities through the lens of the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).</narrative>
  </description>
